  "body": "Hi @agriggio \n\nI recently reported a bug in nind-denoise's denoise_image.py that causes a crash with a ValueError when processing images whose dimensions don't divide evenly by the tile size. The fix was submitted as PR #11 to the upstream trougnouf/nind-denoise repo and initially appeared to be merged on April 16, however the fix was not actually present in the resulting code, so apparently the merge had not been applied correctly.\n\nI flagged this to trougnouf who investigated and re-applied the patch today (May 5, 2026). I have verified by cloning the upstream repo and confirming the fixed lines are now present in src/nind_denoise/denoise_image.py.\n\nYour fork at agriggio/nind-denoise is currently 1 commit behind the upstream. You may want to pull the latest changes so ART users who clone your fork get the fix automatically.\n\nThe relevant upstream commit is: https://github.com/trougnouf/nind-denoise/commit/272428e\n\nThanks for maintaining the ART integration — it's a great tool.",
